The section carried more fiction than fact. Found by reading it against the
data rather than looking at it:

Fabricated outright
- Five hardcoded "Benachrichtigungen": "Projekt Bad Hersfeld - Nachforderung
  von ITK · vor 12 Min", "Zustimmung erteilt für Frankfurt Hbf (EEA)",
  "Deadline überschritten: Köln Messe/Deutz", "Neues Projekt angelegt: München
  Ost", "Neue Excel-Datei hochgeladen: 47 Projekte". Two of them name stations
  outside RB Mitte entirely.
- A Microsoft 365 card with a pulsing green "connected" dot and three
  "Verfügbar" labels. There was no integration: @azure/msal-browser and
  @azure/msal-react were dependencies with no code, no Graph call existed
  anywhere, and both buttons only raised a toast saying the feature "wird in
  Kürze aktiviert". Card, dialog, connect button and both packages removed.
- "API: Verbunden" with a green pulse, on a static SPA whose vercel.json
  declares no functions and whose data comes from localStorage.
- "Version 2.4.1 • Build: Production" against a package.json reading 2.0.0 —
  the same drift already fixed in the footer. Now __APP_VERSION__.

Six buttons that lied to the audit trail
- "Status-Update an alle Projektleiter", "Outlook-Termin erstellen", "In
  Teams-Kanal posten", "Kritische Fälle eskalieren", the per-notification
  "Senden", and the per-deadline "Erinnerung" all wrote an audit entry saying
  the work had happened and then did nothing. "Kritische Fälle eskaliert -
  N kritische Projekte eskaliert" put a false escalation record into the very
  trail the Änderungshistorie reads. All replaced with four buttons that
  navigate where their label says.
- "Aktualisieren" recorded "Manuelle Synchronisierung ausgelöst" and
  synchronised nothing; it now genuinely invalidates the query cache.

Wrong rather than invented
- "Anstehende Deadlines" was `projects.filter(has any pruefDatum).slice(0,12)`
  with no sort, so it showed twelve arbitrary projects, not the nearest
  deadlines. A review without a date fell back to the literal string
  "2026-06-15", which is why every row showed the same date, and an unknown
  reviewer rendered as "Unbekannt". It is now every open review that actually
  carries a Prüfdatum, soonest first, with German dates, the department, an
  overdue marker, and the reviewer omitted when there is none.
- The old fake notifications are replaced by Handlungsbedarf, counted from the
  18,172 review rows: 558 Prüftermine überschritten, 132 abgelehnt oder
  gestoppt, 97 Nachforderungen offen, 111 offen ohne Prüfer.

Layout
- The quick-action labels were clipped mid-word ("Kritische Fälle" in the
  screenshot) because shadcn's Button base sets whitespace-nowrap. They wrap
  now. Card grid 5 -> 4 after the Microsoft card was removed; measured 0
  cards overflowing the viewport and 0 overflowing internally.

Two e2e assertions guard it: the dashboard must contain none of the ten
invented strings, and every Schnellaktion must land on its route.

Gates: 0 type errors, 129 passed / 6 skipped, 80 lint warnings, verify-data
clean, build clean, e2e 22 passed / 0 failed.

